{% comment %}
  Renders an empty, JS-populated vertical dot rail that jumps between the
  homepage's own sections and highlights whichever one is in view.

  Built entirely from the live DOM at runtime (see assets/scroll-rail.js)
  instead of a hardcoded anchor list, so it automatically follows whatever
  sections actually exist in whatever order the merchant has them in —
  add, remove, or reorder a section in the theme editor and the rail just
  reflects it, nothing to keep in sync by hand.

  Usage:
  {% render 'scroll-rail' %}
{% endcomment %}
{{ 'component-scroll-rail.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<nav class="scroll-rail" id="ScrollRail" aria-label="Section progress" hidden></nav>
<script src="{{ 'scroll-rail.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
